1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,830
Google's quantum chip just threw away 92 percent of its work.
谷歌的量子芯片，刚刚把92%的成果扔掉了。

2
00:00:03,830 --> 00:00:04,580
On purpose.
故意的。

3
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:05,830
And that's the good news.
而且这是个好消息。

4
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:07,350
It made the journal Science.
登上了《科学》杂志。

5
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:09,190
Today's question: how does a computer
今天的问题：一台电脑，

6
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:11,050
get better by throwing things away?
怎么靠“扔东西”变强？

7
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:11,750
Meet Qubie.
认识一下小比特。

8
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:15,080
Qubie is a qubit, and Qubie is very, very fragile.
它是一个量子比特，非常非常脆弱。

9
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,080
A normal bit is like a light switch:
普通的比特像电灯开关：

10
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:17,860
zero or one.
0 或者 1。

11
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:19,760
A qubit is more like a spinning coin:
量子比特更像一枚旋转的硬币：

12
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,410
a bit of both, until you look.
看之前，两样都沾一点。

13
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:23,190
But a little heat or a little noise,
可一点点热、一点点噪声，

14
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,900
and the coin wobbles off course.
硬币就转歪了。

15
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,750
That's an error.
这就是错误。

16
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,790
And quantum chips make lots of them.
量子芯片犯的错可多了。

17
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:29,950
So Google groups many qubits together
所以谷歌把很多量子比特编成一组，

18
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:32,230
to act like one sturdy logical qubit.
当一个结实的“逻辑比特”用。

19
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:33,310
Like a group of friends
就像一群朋友，

20
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:35,200
remembering one phone number together.
一起记一个电话号码。

21
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,690
Twist one: the team is great at the easy moves,
反转一：这一组人做简单动作很拿手，

22
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:38,820
but not every move.
但不是所有动作都行。

23
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:40,280
To compute anything at all,
想算任何题目，

24
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,120
it needs one special ingredient.
还缺一样特殊材料。

25
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,900
Physicists call it a magic state.
物理学家管它叫“魔法态”。

26
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,420
Yes, that's the real name.
没错，真叫这个名字。

27
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,220
Think of it as the yeast in bread:
就像面包里的酵母：

28
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,720
without it, nothing rises.
没有它，面发不起来。

29
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,320
The problem: fresh magic states come out messy,
麻烦是：魔法态刚做出来，

30
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:52,280
full of errors.
总是乱糟糟的，全是错。

31
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:55,430
The old fix is called distillation: make lots of messy ones,
老办法叫“蒸馏”：做一大堆烂的，

32
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,610
then boil them down to a few good ones.
再熬成几个好的。

33
00:00:57,610 --> 00:00:59,780
Some estimates say it could eat up
有估算说，它可能要吃掉

34
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:02,960
90 to 95 percent of a quantum computer's qubits.
一台量子计算机90%到95%的比特。

35
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:05,340
Twist two: this time Google tried a new trick
反转二：谷歌这次试了个新办法，

36
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:06,470
called cultivation.
叫“培育”。

37
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:08,460
Grow one magic state in a small patch,
在一小块地方，种出一个魔法态，

38
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:10,300
and keep checking it as it grows.
一边长，一边检查。

39
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,530
If any check looks wrong,
只要有一项检查不对劲，

40
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:12,770
toss it and start over.
扔掉，重来。

41
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:13,750
Like baking cookies,
就像烤饼干，

42
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:16,460
and tossing every one that looks even a little burnt.
稍微有点焦的，统统扔掉。

43
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:18,300
Only about 8 percent survive.
最后只留下大约8%，

44
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:20,140
92 percent go in the trash.
92%进了垃圾桶。

45
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:22,460
But the survivors are excellent:
可留下来的特别好：

46
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:24,240
99.99 percent fidelity.
保真度99.99%。

47
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,470
That's roughly one error
差不多一万次

48
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:26,410
in ten thousand.
才错一次。

49
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:28,130
Compared with no cultivation,
比不培育的，

50
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:29,850
errors drop about 40 times.
错误少了大约40倍。

51
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:31,780
And it fits in a small corner of the chip,
而且它只占芯片的一个小角落，

52
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:33,330
instead of most of the machine.
不用占掉大半台机器。

53
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:34,790
Twist three, the weird part:
反转三，最反直觉：

54
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:37,350
throwing away is cheap. Mistakes are expensive.
扔掉很便宜，犯错很贵。

55
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:38,950
A failed try wastes a blink.
失败一次，只浪费一眨眼。

56
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:41,710
One hidden error can ruin a whole calculation.
藏着一个错，能毁掉整道题。

57
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:42,720
That's why factories
这就是为什么工厂

58
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,870
check the parts before building the car.
先检查零件，再装汽车。

59
00:01:44,870 --> 00:01:46,330
The chip is called Willow.
这块芯片叫 Willow。

60
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:50,090
Google says it's the first time cultivation ran on real hardware.
谷歌说，这是培育第一次在真硬件上跑通。

61
00:01:50,090 --> 00:01:52,360
Friendly fine print: this is one ingredient,
友情提示：这只是一样材料，

62
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:54,130
not a finished quantum computer.
不是一台造好的量子计算机。

63
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:56,440
Truly useful quantum computers still need
真正有用的量子计算机，

64
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,240
many more, much better qubits.
还需要多得多、好得多的比特。

65
00:01:58,240 --> 00:01:59,350
So no, it won't crack
所以不，它明天

66
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:00,670
your password tomorrow.
破解不了你的密码。

67
00:02:00,670 --> 00:02:02,230
Qubie passed every check.
小比特通过了检查。

68
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:04,080
Qubie is now unbearable.
现在它骄傲得不得了。

